      "created_at": "2023-04-05T17:31:46Z",
      "updated_at": "2023-04-05T17:31:46Z",
      "body": "It's different if memory is allocated exactly once and never released explicitly by Py_Finalize(), or if each Py_Initialize() call allocates new memory. Most of remaining \"leaks\" are memory allocated exactly once and then never released by Py_Finalize().\r\n\r\nThere is still a work-in-progress to convert remaining stdlib extensions to multi-phase initialization. A recent example with _elementtree: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/fee7a995a18589001a432cea365fd04bf8efb7c1\r\n\r\nIf you are curious, you should dig into the pymain_free() function of Modules/main.c to see memory not freed by Py_Finalize(), but freed by Py_RunMain().",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
